<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bombay State</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> State was a state of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> formed from the former Bombay Province, with its capital at Bombay. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> were merged into it from 1948, and in 1956 it was enlarged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> and Kutch. In 1960 it was divided along linguistic lines into Gujarat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, the successors of the princely states that joined it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bombay-state.jpg" alt="Bombay State" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Superbenjamin this file: Furfur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bombay_in_India_(1951).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
